Thus we need shift_candidate_alpha prepared (we will have). Also need loading_container_available (we have loading_container_alpha available initially). After loading, loading_container_loaded becomes true, loading_container_leg_linked set.

Then we need to stage schedule candidate: stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate. We have origin_leg_loaded false (we haven't loaded origin leg). So we can stage.

Then verify loading profile nominal: verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate, candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate, candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_loading_verified ?candidate. We'll have skill_certificate linked (we will assign), operator linked, loading container linked and leg linked, destination_leg_loaded false. So we can verify.

Then establish clearance nominal: establish_clearance_nominal requires candidate_loading_verified ?candidate, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established. We'll have compliance_certificate linked (we will assign). So we can establish clearance.

Then we need route_sequence_context_set? Actually establish_clearance_nominal does not set route_sequence_context_set. So we need to set it via something else? There is establish_clearance_origin_loaded etc which set route_sequence_context_set. But we can use finalize_candidate_direct which requires candidate_clearance_established and not route_sequence_context_set. So we can use finalize_candidate_direct after clearance established, without needing route_sequence_context_set. That will set candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready.

Thus after establishing clearance nominal, we can run finalize_candidate_direct on shift_candidate_alpha to get dispatch_ready and candidate_finalized.

Then allocate dispatch slot: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate. We have dispatch_ready after finalize_candidate_direct. candidate_task_profile_linked true. dispatch_slot_available we have dispatch_slot_alpha. So we can allocate.

Then execute schedule dispatch: execute_schedule_dispatch requires dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?candidate. After allocate, we have dispatch_allocated and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked set. We also need candidate_vehicle_linked (we set via allocate_vehicle_unit). So we can execute.

Thus shift_candidate_alpha dispatched.

Now for origin_availability_alpha dispatch:

