Thus after shift_candidate_alpha dispatch, dispatch_slot_available becomes true again.

Thus we can allocate dispatch slot for origin_availability_alpha, then execute_origin_dispatch.

execute_origin_dispatch requires dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability, candidate_vehicle_linked ?origin_availability ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?origin_availability ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?origin_availability.

We need to allocate vehicle to origin_availability_alpha (we already did). So candidate_vehicle_linked true.

Thus we can execute.

Now goal also requires candidate_created shift_candidate_beta (we will create early). compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha remains true (we never used it? Actually we will assign compliance_certificate to shift_candidate_alpha via assign_compliance_certificate, which will make compliance_certificate_available false. Then after we finish, we may need to release it to make it available again for goal. The goal requires compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha. So we must ensure it is available at the end. If we assign it to shift_candidate_alpha, we need to release it after use. There is release_compliance_certificate action.

